description:
Design a Pulse Width Modulation (PWM) generator. The module outputs a signal, ofState, that toggles based on a comparison between an 8-bit counter and an 8-bit duty cycle value (dutyCount). Each clock cycle increments the counter, and when the counter is less than dutyCount, ofState is set HIGH; otherwise, it is set LOW. This effectively allows for control of the duty cycle in PWM applications, where a higher dutyCount results in a longer HIGH signal duration relative to the total period.
module top_module(
    clk,
    dutyCount,
    ofState
);

code:
module top_module(
    clk,
    dutyCount,
    ofState
);input clk;
input [7:0] dutyCount;
output ofState;
reg ofState;

reg [7:0] counter = 0;



always @(posedge clk) begin: PWM_LOGIC
    counter <= (counter + 1);
    ofState <= (counter < dutyCount);
end

endmodule

