Design a circuit that functions as a 1-bit carry save adder (CSA). The module takes three single-bit inputs (INa, INb, INc) and outputs a single-bit sum (SUM) and a carry output (COUT). The SUM is computed using exclusive OR operations on the inputs, while the COUT is determined by assessing the conditions under which a carry is generated among the input bits. This configuration allows for efficient addition of multiple binary values in a way that optimizes for carry propagation.
