description:
Design a 3-bit binary to Gray code converter. The module takes a 3-bit binary input and outputs its corresponding 3-bit Gray code representation. The first bit of Gray code is derived directly from the most significant bit of the binary input, while the subsequent bits are generated by XORing the current binary bit with the previous one, allowing for effective conversion between these two coding schemes.
module top_module(
    input [2:0] bin_in,
    output reg [2:0] gray_out
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [2:0] bin_in,
    output reg [2:0] gray_out
);always @(*) begin
        gray_out[0] = bin_in[0] ^ bin_in[1];
        gray_out[1] = bin_in[1] ^ bin_in[2];
        gray_out[2] = bin_in[2];
    end

endmodule

