description:
Design a debouncing circuit that stabilizes a noisy input signal. The module takes a clock input and a one-bit noisy signal as input and produces a clean output signal. It counts clock cycles to determine if the input has been stable long enough to change the output state. If the input differs from the output, it increments a counter until it reaches a specified threshold (100,000 clock cycles) before toggling the output state, effectively filtering out any short-duration noise. If the input remains steady, the counter resets to zero, ensuring that only sustained changes are registered.
module top_module(
	input clk,
    input in,
    output reg out=0
    );

code:
module top_module(
	input clk,
    input in,
    output reg out=0
    );reg [31:0] cnt=0;
	always@(posedge clk)
		begin
			if(in!=out)
				begin
					cnt=cnt+1;

					if(cnt==100000)
					begin
						out=~out;
						cnt=0;
					end

				end
			else cnt=0;

		end
endmodule

