Design a reset recovery circuit that utilizes a clock signal and an asynchronous reset input. When the reset (RST) signal is asserted low, the output Reset and internal signal mid are set to low. On subsequent clock cycles, if RST is high, the internal signal mid is set high, which then propagates to set the Reset output to high as well. This circuit ensures that the Reset output is appropriately synchronized with the clock while responding to the reset signal.
